# New Domain & Server Installation Guide
This guide outlines the step-by-step procedure for deploying the Pinellas Credit Union application to a new domain and initializing the database.

---

## 1. Domain & Web Hosting Configuration (Hostinger)
When migrating to your new domain on Hostinger, make sure the server pointing is correct:

1. **Add Domain to Hostinger**: Log in to your Hostinger hPanel and add the new domain name.
2. **Set Document Root**: In the domain's website settings, configure the document root to point to the `public/` directory of the project (e.g., `/public_html/public/`), NOT the root folder.
3. **SSL Certificate**: Generate and force an active SSL certificate for the new domain (`https://`).

---

## 2. Git Setup & Deployment
You can either continue using your existing Git repository or create a new one.

### Option A: Reuse Existing Git Repository (Recommended)
You can continue using the current GitHub repository (`https://github.com/ffcu-pinellas/pinellas.git`).
To connect it to your new Hostinger domain:
1. Go to your Hostinger hPanel -> **Git** under your website section.
2. Add your repository URL (`https://github.com/ffcu-pinellas/pinellas.git`) and branch (`main`).
3. Set up the Webhook URL provided by Hostinger inside your GitHub repository settings under **Webhooks** to enable auto-deployment when you push changes.

### Option B: Set up a New Git Repository
If you choose to set up a brand new GitHub repository:
1. Create a new repository on GitHub (e.g. `https://github.com/username/new-repo.git`).
2. Inside your local project directory, update the remote target URL:
   ```bash
   git remote set-url origin https://github.com/username/new-repo.git
   ```
3. Push your code to the new repository:
   ```bash
   git push -u origin main
   ```
4. Set up the deployment link in Hostinger using your new repository URL.

---

## 3. Environment Configuration (`.env`)
Create a `.env` file on the new server (usually by copying `.env.example` or your current `.env` file) and update these parameters:

```env
APP_NAME="Digital Bank"
APP_ENV=production
APP_KEY=base64:mzw8xiKnl5Z0zb/ggmlPhWJ/mfQqi3JPfcXuyrXkIqk=
APP_DEBUG=false
APP_DEMO=false

# Update with your new domain URL
APP_URL=https://your-new-domain.com/

# Update database credentials for the new server
DB_CONNECTION=mysql
DB_HOST=127.0.0.1
DB_PORT=3306
DB_DATABASE=your_new_database_name
DB_USERNAME=your_new_database_user
DB_PASSWORD=your_new_database_password

# Session Settings - Update to match the new domain (note the leading dot)
SESSION_DOMAIN=.your-new-domain.com
SESSION_SECURE_COOKIE=true
```

---

## 4. Database Initialization & Seeding
This project has a dedicated **Web-Based Migration Runner** so you do not need terminal (Artisan) access to setup your database schema.

Once your code is deployed to the new domain and your `.env` is updated:
1. Open your browser and navigate to:
   ```text
   https://your-new-domain.com/deploy/run-migration
   ```
2. This script will automatically run in the background and:
   - Perform all standard Laravel database migrations.
   - Run core index additions and database fixes (for `document_histories`, cards, and remote deposits).
   - Create transaction security and card tables.
   - Seed **30+ core email and bank templates** (Zelle, Chase, Wells Fargo, etc.) in the database.
   - Seed the new **Welcome Member Email Template** under the `welcome_letter` category in the document templates section.
3. Once completed, you will see a success message: `Migration Successful!...`

---

## 5. Welcome Member Email Customization
The Welcome Email is fully dynamic and manageable by administrators.

To view or customize the welcome email template:
1. Log in to the Admin Panel.
2. Navigate to **Document Templates** under the management menu.
3. Look for the template categorized under `welcome_letter` (named **Pinellas FCU Welcome Letter**).
4. Click **Edit** to update the text, header description, physical address, or routing numbers directly from the WYSIWYG editor.

### Supported Template Placeholders (Shortcodes)
When sending welcome letters, the system automatically parses these tags:
- `[[FULL_NAME]]` - The user's registered name.
- `[[CHECKING_ACCOUNT_NUMBER]]` - The user's checking account number.
- `[[SAVINGS_ACCOUNT_NUMBER]]` - The user's savings account number.
- `[[ROUTING_NUMBER]]` - The global bank routing number.
- `[[LOGIN_URL]]` - Direct link to the login page.
- `[[LOGO_URL]]` - Absolute branding logo link.
- `[[SITE_TITLE]]` - Site title setting.
- `[[HOME_URL]]` - Base domain URL.
